===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To work as a tinker.
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[fiddle]] with something in an [[attempt]] to [[fix]], [[mend]] or [[improve]] it, especially in an [[experimental]] or [[unskilled]] manner.
#* '''1894''', {{w|Thomas Hardy}}, ''A Few Crusted Characters''
#*: the broken bureau-lock and '''tinkered''' window-pane
#* {{quote-journal
|1=en
|date=2012-01
|author=Robert M. Pringle
|title=How to Be Manipulative
|volume=100
|issue=1
|page=31
|magazine=[[w:American Scientist|American Scientist]]
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/1/how-to-be-manipulative
|passage=As in much of biology, the most satisfying truths in ecology derive from manipulative experimentation. '''Tinker''' with nature and quantify how it responds.
|accessdate=11 May 2013
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20131003094045/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/1/how-to-be-manipulative
|archivedate=3 October 2013
}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Eric Goulard|title=Body Language Secrets Revealed|passage=And because he wants to show that he is a dominant male, he '''tinkered''' the engine of his motorbike to make it even noisier.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 May 20|title=Network News: LNER seeks innovation through FutureLabs project|journal=Rail|page=14|text=We're not just talking about changes that '''tinker''' around the edges - we're looking to take advantage of some of the world's latest digital and tech developments to improve our service.}}

